    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1008-a1">

                <pb facs="0776" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg694"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Portuguese Minister for Foreign Affairs to the
                        Minister of Portugal.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-06-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                    1911</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The Constituent National
                    Assembly having solemnly confirmed the change of institutions as proclaimed on
                    October 5, I beg your excellency to be pleased to express to the Government to
                    which you are accredited, at the earliest opportunity, my great satisfaction at
                    the good relations maintained with the Government of the Republic during the
                    period that has just expired, which relations I confidently look upon as a
                    pledge of unalterable friendship between Portugal and that country.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will also avail yourself of the opportunity to confirm the
                    impression of profound gratitude on the part of the Portuguese Nation for that
                    Government’s prompt and final recognition of the Republic.</p>
                <p>Greetings and fraternity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bernardino
                    Machado.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
